Deployment Playbook


1.Initialize Project & Inject Role Contexts:Platform Engineer.

Start by creating the repository and defining Claude's operational parameters.
Scaffold base framework (e.g., Vite + React/TypeScript).
Place three skill.md files into a .claude/ or docs/ directory in the project root.
Initialize Claude Code in the terminal and explicitly map the roles:Claude, read the skill files in ./docs. 
For all infrastructure and state questions, use platform-engineer-skill.md. 
For component generation, use ui-ux-engineer-skill.md. For auth and data handling, use security-engineer-skill.md.

2.Establish Figma MCP Connection & Extract Tokens:UI/UX Engineer.
Connect Claude directly to your Figma environment to pull the design system without manual translation.
Start the Figma MCP server: claude mcp add --transport http figma [https://mcp.figma.com/mcp](https://mcp.figma.com/mcp)Authenticate via /mcp.
Instruct Claude using the UI/UX persona:Acting as the UI/UX Engineer, read the Figma variables from [URL].
 Generate a comprehensive design token file (e.g., tailwind.config.ts) mapping all typography, color palettes, and spacing rules.

 3.Scaffold the Component Library:UI/UX Engineer.
 Build the UI system from the atom level up, ensuring reusable components match your design specifications.
 Feed Claude specific Figma node URLs for atomic elements (buttons, inputs, modals).
 Prompt: Acting as the UI/UX Engineer, parse node [URL] and generate a responsive, accessible React component using our design tokens.

 4.Implement Identity, Auth & Security Boundaries:Security Engineer.Before wiring application logic, establish the security perimeter—especially critical for applications handling sensitive or enterprise data.Point Claude to the Figma frames detailing your authentication flows, single sign-on (SSO), and multi-factor authentication (MFA) screens.

 Prompt: Acting as the Security Engineer, implement the SSO and MFA login flows based on [URL].
 Instruct Claude to configure Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) routing boundaries and set up secure, HTTP-only cookie handling for JWTs.
 Have Claude generate strict Content Security Policy (CSP) headers for the production build.

 5.Assemble Page Layouts & API Integrations:Platform Engineer & UI/UX Engineer.Combine the UI components into full page layouts and connect them to your backend services.
Provide Claude with the main application frame URLs.
Prompt: Acting as the UI/UX Engineer, compose the dashboard layout using our component library based on [URL].

Once the UI is built, prompt: Acting as the Platform Engineer, integrate state management to connect this layout to our API gateway. Ensure all API calls handle JWT authentication seamlessly.\

6.Engineer the PWA Architecture:Platform Engineer.
Convert the web application into an installable, offline-capable PWA.
Prompt Claude to generate a fully compliant manifest.json ensuring display: "standalone", proper theme colors, and the required icon arrays.
Instruct Claude to implement Workbox for service worker generation.
Define strict caching strategies:Configure a Stale-While-Revalidate strategy for static assets and a Network-First strategy for API routes.
Implement IndexedDB (e.g., via Dexie.js) for local data persistence so users can interact with the app offline, queueing mutations for when connectivity is restored.

7.Audit & Finalize Production Build:Security Engineer.

Verify the build against production standards before deployment.
Run a local build: npm run build.
Instruct Claude: Acting as the Security Engineer, audit the build output and source code for exposed secrets, missing data encryption in IndexedDB, and proper error boundary fallback UI.
Run Lighthouse via CLI and have Claude resolve any accessibility (a11y) or PWA capability deductions.